Z||000004||DrRodey||09-30-2001||04:36 PM||||Thats beautiful work.. Now ... HOW'D YOU DO IT!!?????!! <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/confused.gif"> <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/confused.gif">||||reg||1
Z||000005||DaRkLoRD||09-30-2001||04:45 PM||||   <IMG SRC="http://www.digitalfusion.on.ca/transfer/sil3.jpg">   <P>there's another one..<P>The technique I use, is to create a layer mask over the car, covering only the body panels.. then I fill this layer with whatever color I'd like to change the car to, and set that layer mode to <B>HUE</B><BR>Then to make it darker if I wanted, I make another layer, and fill the same mask shape with white, set that layer mode to <B>LUMINOCITY</B>, and then adjust the opacity to get the color I'm looking for.<P>I still haven't figured out how to make a car yellow, or change a colored car to a black one.. Aus, help??    <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/biggrin.gif"><P>------------------<BR>      <A HREF="mailto:steve@fieroproject.com">steve@fieroproject.com</A>      <BR><A HREF="http://www.fieroproject.com" TARGET=_blank>http://www.fieroproject.com</A><p>[This message has been edited by DaRkLoRD (edited 09-30-2001).]||||reg||3
Z||000006||DaRkLoRD||09-30-2001||05:08 PM||||ok, it's not perfect but you get the idea...<P> <IMG SRC="http://www.digitalfusion.on.ca/transfer/sil4.jpg"> <P>------------------<BR>    <A HREF="mailto:steve@fieroproject.com">steve@fieroproject.com</A>    <BR><A HREF="http://www.fieroproject.com" TARGET=_blank>http://www.fieroproject.com</A>||||reg||6
