Z||000012||DaRkLoRD||09-30-2001||09:03 PM||||I have quite a number of Photoshop tutorials on my website already, I guess I'll make one for this too.  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/smile.gif"><P>give me a couple of days, and I should have precise instructions with step by step pictures.. though I would like to find out how to make a car yellow or bright orange, that hasn't worked yet.<P>------------------<BR>    <A HREF="mailto:steve@fieroproject.com">steve@fieroproject.com</A>    <BR><A HREF="http://www.fieroproject.com" TARGET=_blank>http://www.fieroproject.com</A>||||reg||3
Z||000013||Sootah||09-30-2001||09:16 PM||||So far my biggest problem has been changing the color to black, I always lose the highlights and it looks like I did it in paint. So I'd just be your biggest fan if you wrote up a good color tweak tut.<P>Thanx,<BR>-<I><B>Sootah</B></I><P>------------------<BR>  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/Sootah__Nuclear_Happy_Face_Sig.jpg">  <BR><sup><I>Never pull your pants down in Cosco, the dang monkeys will getcha</I></sup> <BR><sup><B>AIM</B>: KSSouter</sup>||||reg||1
Z||000014||DaRkLoRD||09-30-2001||09:59 PM||||ok.. to get a black car:<P>once you have the mask, create a new layer and fill the selection with black. Set this layer mode to <B>DARKEN</B>, and then duplicate this layer, and invert the colors so it's totally white... set this new layer to <B>HUE</B>, and then tweak the settings on both those layers.. you'll also need to play with the contrast of the original layer, I made a copy of this so I'd still have the original layer.<P>Soon I'll write this up in more detail and include pictures.  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/smile.gif"> but in the meantime, if there are any questions, just ask..<P>------------------<BR>    <A HREF="mailto:steve@fieroproject.com">steve@fieroproject.com</A>    <BR><A HREF="http://www.fieroproject.com" TARGET=_blank>http://www.fieroproject.com</A>||||reg||3
Z||000015||DaRkLoRD||09-30-2001||10:02 PM||||another thing, the more color the car has, the better the final product turns out with this technique... I tried it on Loki's gold SE, and since it was a rather dull picture (overcast day..) the new colors were very washed out.<BR>but even in a greyish picture, a red car will work better than silver, gold or white..<P>------------------<BR>    <A HREF="mailto:steve@fieroproject.com">steve@fieroproject.com</A>    <BR><A HREF="http://www.fieroproject.com" TARGET=_blank>http://www.fieroproject.com</A>||||reg||4
Z||000016||FieroHeather||09-30-2001||10:09 PM||||Woah!  Great work there dude!!<P>Maybe you should try to get a job at a place where they would appreciate your genius  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/biggrin.gif">  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/biggrin.gif">  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/biggrin.gif">  Ok, maybe your talent then!<P>No one has ever created a pink fiero for me as of yet.  Salmon pink, not bubblegum...||||reg||6
